Notices and attribution
=======================

This repository is an independent reimplementation. No source code was copied
from any other project. The architecture was studied from public documentation:

- starling-client/starling (MIT, https://github.com/starling-client/starling):
  the native-mod build flow (a player's mods are sealed, a CI job compiles the
  game with them in a sandbox, a second job publishes the result). The general
  shape of that flow is credited here. Starling is MIT licensed; this project
  shares architecture only and no Starling source text.
- starling-client/mod-builds (no license file): the public README of that
  repository documents the service design (job ids as content addresses of
  version+commit+body, sealed request assets, a base build cache, per-address
  quotas). This project follows that public design with original code and its
  own wording. Any similarity is architectural and intentional; no code was
  taken from that repository.
- horizon-mixins (MIT, https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon-mixins) by
  levzzz5154: the mixin tool used to apply native mod bundles to Horizon's
  source at build time. It is installed at a pinned revision
  (ddd9700b21997c95d95ac6ee5ecafe3830cf622a) by the base workflow.
- Horizon (https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon) by horizon-rust and its
  contributors: the game this service recompiles. The Android fork built here
  is ProSteve123GH/horizon-android-old.

This project is a personal, unofficial build service. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or connected to Starling, horizon-rust, or Mojang.
